# /small (ino 8) claims THE ROOT DIRECTORY'S block.  Block 5 is not a guess: it is the
# first data block (s_isize -- one superblock plus four i-list blocks on this 200-block
# volume), and mkfs allocates the root's directory block first, so this spec cannot drift
# when the manifest changes.  It reaches phase 1's DUP, the phase 1b rescan that only a dup
# provokes, phase 2's DUP/BAD entry removal, phase 4's clri(), and then the free-list
# salvage -- /small's own block is left accounted for nowhere.
i8.addr0=5
